{title: 433 - Ten Thousand Times Ten Thousand}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #433 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 433}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Ten thousand [C/E]times [D#dim]ten [G/D]thousand,
[G]In [Bm]sparkling [Em/B]raiment bright,
[Bm]The [F#m/C#]armies [D/A]of [Am]the [A#m]ransomed [Am/C]saints
[Em/B]Throng [D/A]up the [Em]steeps [G]of [D/F#]light.
[D]'Tis finished, [G]all [Am/E]is [G]finished,
[G#m]Their [Am]fight [F#dim]with [G]death and sin.
[D]Fling open wide [G]the golden [Em]gates,
[Am/E]And [Em/B]let [Bm]the victors [Em/B]in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]What [C/E]rush of [Em]hallelujahs
[G]Fills [Bm]all the [Em/B]earth [Am/C]and [Em/B]sky!
[Bm]The [F#m/C#]ringing [D/A]of [Am]a [A#m]thousand [Am/C]harps
[Em/B]Proclaims [D/F#]the [Em]triumph [G]high.
[D]O day for [G]which [Am/E]creation
[G#m]And [Am]all [F#dim]its [G]tribes were made!
[D]O [Em]joy, [D]for [G]all its [Am/E]former woes
[Am/E]A [Em/B]thousandfold [Am/C]repaid!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O [C/E]then what [Em]raptured [G/D]greetings
[G]On [Bm]Canaan's [Em/B]happy shore!
[Bm]What [F#m/C#]knitting [D/A]severed [A#m]friendship [Am/C]where
[Em/B]Death [D/A]partings [Em]are [G]no [D/F#]more!
[D]Then eyes with [G]joy [Am/E]shall [G]sparkle,
[G#m]That [Am]brimmed [F#dim]with [G]tears of late;
[D]Orphans no [G]longer [Am/E]fatherless,
[Am/E]Nor [Em/B]widows [Bm/D]desolate.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Bring [C/E]near Thy [Em]great [D#dim]salvation,
[G]Thou [Bm]Lamb for [Em/B]sinners slain,
[Bm]Fill [F#m/C#]up [Am]the [D/A]roll [Am]of [A#m]Thine [Bm]elect,
[Em/B]Then take [D/A]Thy power [G]and [D/F#]reign!
[D]Appear, Desire [Am/E]of [G]nations,
[G#m]Thine [Am]exiles [G]long for home;
[D]Show in [Em]the [D]heavens [G/D]Thy [Am/E]promised sign;
[Am/E]Thou [Em/B]Prince [Bm]and Savior [Em/B]come!
{end_of_verse}
